Keep -Wunused-but-set-global a warning with newer clang.

Pango builds with -Werror=unused-but-set-variable.  The clang of the zedBSD
toolchain (LLVM 23) puts -Wunused-but-set-global in that group and reports
the parent_class variable that G_DEFINE_TYPE defines in files that do not
chain up, so pango-fontset.c and others stopped.  That one diagnostic stays
a warning, as it is in GLib's own build.  (The getc_unlocked fallback this
patch also had in WS115 p007 went when the C library gained the function.)

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -145,6 +145,9 @@
     '-Werror=empty-body',
     '-Werror=write-strings',
     '-Werror=unused-but-set-variable',
+    # Newer clang counts an unused G_DEFINE_TYPE parent_class, a file-scope
+    # variable, in the group above; it stays a warning, as elsewhere.
+    '-Wno-error=unused-but-set-global',
     '-Wundef', # FIXME: https://bugzilla.gnome.org/show_bug.cgi?id=792481
   ]
 
